  "voice": {
    "engine": "gemini",
    "model": "gemini-2.5-flash-preview-tts",
    "name": "Sadaltager",
    "style": "You are a friendly senior engineer showing a curious developer how a magic trick is really done: what LangGraph adds to an AI agent. Talk, don't read: calm, clear teaching delivery with real pitch movement, about two and a half words per second, short natural pauses between steps. Open with real urgency on 'Your AI agent just refunded a customer', then a beat, and land 'Nobody approved it' flatly, like bad news. Read the customer's email, 'I was charged twice', like quoting a real message. Keep 'Step one, step two, step three' crisp and brisk. Slow down on the reveal: 'the whole graph stops' and 'It waits until someone answers' should feel like a held breath. Smile on 'Approved by you.' Take a short breath before 'Now, here's the catch' and say the catch calmly and seriously, never scary. Warm on the recap. Say LangGraph as 'Lang Graph' and LangChain as 'Lang Chain'. Clear, global English. Never hyped, never robotic. Read every word exactly as written."
